#N canvas 20 20 5200 5200 12;
#X text 20 20 u_net -- the phone status link \, and the sole owner of the fourth display surface. It consumes disp like the g_ files and forwards what a phone can show over UDP OSC \; inbound it takes a closed vocabulary of five commands. It writes err and presence \, and nothing else may learn a phone exists. ref/device/phone.md, f 58;
#X text 700 20 creation arg 1: the phone's host \, the fallback when phone-ip.sh finds none. arg 2: its OSC receive port \, 8000 for TouchOSC \, never 9000 (its WebDAV) or 4001-4003 (mother's). arg 3: this end's inbound UDP port \, 9001 on the device and different on the Mac. inlet 1: a bang from u_map that flips test mode. inlet 2: c_steps' drum screen state \, 41 numbers. outlet 1: the Volca \, outlet 2: the SP-404 \, both selector-prefixed and wired in u_root (C-2). outlet 3: u_inject \, a checklist's Send line from the phone. outlet 4: c_steps \, the drum screen's sync \, snap \, select <n> \, num and den <-1 or 1> \, and drunk \, skip and move <0-100>., f 58;
#X text 1400 20 State \, never events: every message carries the whole value \, so a dropped datagram is corrected by the next., f 58;
#X text 20 220 Fire and forget: no handshake and no retry \, so the instrument plays the same with no phone. Only the connection retries \, below., f 58;
#X text 700 220 The reserved selectors are matched and left unconnected \, or they would fall out of the reject as parameters. Same order as g_oled's route. diag was appended \, not slotted in: an argument anywhere else renumbers every outlet after it \, the reject included., f 58;
#X text 1400 220 The meters and the grid are dropped: the meters are the disp bus's whole resting traffic and the phone does not draw them \, and grid is the Launchpad's vocabulary., f 58;
#X obj 20 520 r disp;
#X obj 20 570 route in-l in-r status modal modal-off alert led grid diag;
#X obj 560 660 list append;
#X obj 560 1010 oscformat cutit status;
#X obj 560 1060 s \$0-osc;
#X text 300 1150 status is rate-limited too: u_tempo writes the BPM into the footer \, so a knob-1 sweep floods it (ref/device/phone.md). One slot \, as there is only ever one status., f 44;
