#X text 3300 1660 A row in the text is the dirty bit: the flush sends every row and clears the text \, so an idle tick loops zero times \, and a name written twice between ticks sends only its last value., f 58;
#X text 2350 1560 One moses decides update or append: a hit is the row to overwrite \, and a miss \, -1 \, becomes text size \, which appends. C-8, f 58;
#X text 2350 1180 50 ms is the whole rate limit: faster costs datagrams \, slower makes a fader lag on the phone., f 44;
