#X text 20 3880 The inbound vocabulary is closed: six commands and two device names \, all literal route arguments \, and everything else dropped by an unconnected reject. drums alone passes on whatever follows it \, and c_steps refuses a command it does not know as bad-selector (Brendan \, 2026-11-04). netreceive in 0.49 cannot tell who sent a datagram (Reference \, pure-data)., f 66;
#X text 660 3880 The listen is armed at 2000 ms \, C-9 for a socket: a second bind of one UDP port prints an error \, and the silence gate quits at about 735 ms. The port is \$3 \, so object boxes again., f 66;
#X text 1300 3880 The device is m_404 \, never 404: route parses 404 as a float \, and the name arrives as a symbol (Reference \, pure-data)., f 66;
#X text 1940 3880 The ack makes the phone's button flash \, so the flash means received. Each branch fires its action off the trigger's right outlet and the ack off its left., f 66;
#X text 2580 3880 Two outlets \, as u_map has (C-2): the Volca \, then the SP-404. Outlet order is x position \, which is why appending these boxes was safe. The probe is middle C for 200 ms on the Volca \, and pad 1 at velocity 100 on the SP-404., f 66;
#X text 3220 3880 A missing port is made loud: an absent \$3 would listen on 0 in silence \, so moses 1 sends it to err. C-8, f 66;
